Here is a complete, standalone implementation of an LRU (Least Recently Used) cache in Rust.

It uses `std::collections::HashMap` for O(1) lookups and a custom **Doubly Linked List** (implemented using `Vec` indices) to manage the order of usage in O(1) without using `unsafe` code or external crates.

